# ---------------- SpellData.events (Task 9 E3: spell data table) ----------------
# Spell definitions, data-driven. `cast "Fireball"` reads these numbers: it spends `my Mana`,
# refuses while the spell's own cooldown is live, then clones <Spell>Bullet at the caster (or at
# `cast "..." at <thing>`) with the spell's damage/blast/speed/life stamped onto the bullet, plus
# `my Element` so E4's resistance messages have something to read.
#
# A spell with an EMPTY Bullet has no projectile: `cast` sends the message "cast <Spell>" to the
# target (or to the caster for a self spell) and the events decide what happens —
# `when message "cast Heal" arrives` → `add 30 to my health`.
#
# HOW IT LOADS: the file is read when the game loads events (and on hot reload), by name —
# SpellData.events — before any actor's `when me appears` runs, so a spell is complete on the
# first tick. Attaching it to a sheet is optional; the `when game starts` block keeps it valid as
# a normal event file.
#
# FIELDS (per spell, one variable each — the spell name plus the field):
#   <Spell>Mana        mana one cast costs (`my Mana`)
#   <Spell>Cooldown    seconds before the same actor may cast it again
#   <Spell>Damage      damage stamped onto the projectile (`my damage`)
#   <Spell>Blast       explosion radius in cm (`my blast`) — pair with an `explode` bullet sheet
#   <Spell>Element     damage type the projectile carries (`my Element`): fire, cold, poison, ...
#   <Spell>Bullet      actor template the cast clones; empty = the message branch, no projectile
#   <Spell>Speed       projectile speed in cm/s (`my BulletSpeed`)
#   <Spell>Life        projectile lifetime in seconds (`my Life` / `my TimeLeft`)
#   <Spell>Sound       sound played by the caster when it goes off
#
# The bullet template is a scene actor, exactly like `spawn Bullet`: a spell whose template is
# missing warns once when it is first cast. `my <Spell>Cooldown` reads the seconds left, so a HUD
# can `bind FireballLabel to my FireballCooldown`.

when game starts
  # --- Fireball: a damage spell with a projectile ---
  set FireballMana to 10
  set FireballCooldown to 1.2
  set FireballDamage to 20
  set FireballBlast to 180
  set FireballElement to "fire"
  set FireballBullet to "Fireball"
  set FireballSpeed to 420
  set FireballLife to 2.5
  set FireballSound to "fireball"

  # --- Heal: no projectile, the message branch does the work ---
  set HealMana to 15
  set HealCooldown to 2
  set HealDamage to 0
  set HealBlast to 0
  set HealElement to "holy"
  set HealBullet to ""
  set HealSound to "heal"
